// =============================================================================
// Personal tailnet policy
// =============================================================================
// Spliced into tailscale-policy.hujson by tofu/tailscale.tf, at the marker
// named `personal` near the bottom of that file.
//
// THIS IS A FILE-LEVEL SPLIT, NOT A SECOND OWNER. A tailnet has exactly one
// policy document and no include mechanism, so everything here is written to
// the same document, by the same apply, under the same credential. The split
// buys readability and a smaller thing to review — it does not mean tofu leaves
// this alone. Delete a line here and the next apply deletes it from the tailnet.
//
// WHAT BELONGS HERE: settings about devices that are yours and have nothing to
// do with the VPS. What does not: anything keyed on tag:vps, and the tests.
//
// THREE PERSONAL ENTRIES COULD NOT MOVE HERE. A policy document cannot repeat a
// top-level key, and these live in sections the infra file must also define:
// the tag:friends-ssh tagOwner, its acl rule, and its ssh rule. They are marked
// PRE-EXISTING where they sit in tailscale-policy.hujson. Sections that are
// wholly personal — like nodeAttrs — move cleanly; sections that are shared do
// not move at all. That is the whole boundary.
//
// Indented one tab because it is spliced in as a top-level section of that
// document. Read with file() and not templatefile(), so nothing here is
// interpolated — template syntax would survive into the policy as literal text.
// Only tailscale-policy.hujson is a template.

	// CARRIED OVER VERBATIM FROM THE POLICY TOFU REPLACED. None of it is an
	// access rule, all of it is load-bearing, and the resource overwrites the
	// whole document — so anything dropped from this file is deleted on apply.
	//
	//   funnel   the stock grant. Removing it disables Tailscale Funnel
	//            across the tailnet.
	//   mullvad  THIS ATTRIBUTE IS THE MULLVAD EXIT-NODE GATE. These four
	//            addresses are devices with the integration enabled; drop one
	//            and that machine loses its Mullvad exit nodes, with nothing in
	//            the apply output saying so. Targets are raw tailnet addresses
	//            rather than device names because that is how the console wrote
	//            them — left as found, so a diff against the console is a diff
	//            about access and not about formatting.
	"nodeAttrs": [
		{"target": ["autogroup:member"], "attr": ["funnel"]},
		{"target": ["100.108.24.65"], "attr": ["mullvad"]},
		{"target": ["100.111.243.14"], "attr": ["mullvad"]},
		{"target": ["100.95.190.17"], "attr": ["mullvad"]},
		{"target": ["100.90.44.89"], "attr": ["mullvad"]},
	],
